The length of a side of the square is 2 more than the length of this hypotenuse, so  $s=2 + 3\sqrt{2}$. Hence the area of the square is \[
s^{2}=(2+3\sqrt{2})^{2}=\boxed{12 + 8\sqrt{2}}.
\]

Let Earth's radius be $r$.  Since the equator measures 25100 miles, we have $2\pi r = 25100 \Rightarrow r = \frac{12550}{\pi}$.

