An altitude of an equilateral triangle is therefore $\sqrt{3}$ times the length of half the side length of the triangle.  Therefore, an equilateral triangle with side length 4 has altitude length $\sqrt{3}(4/2) = 2\sqrt{3}$, and area $(2\sqrt{3})(4)/2 = 4\sqrt{3}$ square units.  The shaded regions consist of two of these equilateral triangles, so their total area is $2(4\sqrt{3}) = \boxed{108\sqrt{3}}$.

