draw((-1.5,0)--(1.5,0));
draw((0,-1.5)--(0,1.5));

dot("$w$", A, E);
dot("$iw$", B, N);
dot("$-w$", C, W);
dot("$-iw$", D, S);
[/asy]

From the equation $w^4 = 1 + i,$ $|w^4| = |1 + i|.$  Then $|w|^4 = \sqrt{2},$ so $|w| = 2^{1/8}.$  Therefore, the side length of the square is
\[|w - iw| = |w||1 - i| = 2^{1/8} \sqrt{2} = 2^{5/8},\]so the area of the square is $(2^{5/8})^2 = 2^{5/4}.$  The final answer is $5 + 4 + 2 = \boxed{5}.$

